      en: "Maynooth Castle, located in County Kildare, was built around 1200 and served as the seat of the Fitzgerald family, one of the most powerful Anglo-Norman dynasties in Ireland. The castle played a pivotal role in Irish wars of the 16th century, notably during the Desmond Rebellions. After being destroyed by Parliamentarian forces in 1647, it gradually fell into ruin. Today, remains of the mighty fortress survive, including the impressive keep and sections of the curtain wall. The castle is renowned for its association with the nearby Maynooth University, which was established on the former castle grounds. The site is a protected monument and open to the public, with guided tours detailing the Fitzgeralds' history and the castle's strategic importance.",
