      en: "Ballymote Castle in County Sligo is an early 14th-century Norman fortress. Built around 1300, it served as a stronghold for the O'Conchobhair family. It played a significant role in the wars between Anglo-Norman lords and Irish clans. The castle has a pentagonal layout with round towers at the corners. In the 17th century, it was expanded and strengthened but gradually fell into ruin after the siege of 1641. Today, massive walls and towers survive. Ballymote is a National Monument and a popular filming location for historical movies.",
